' 1. Register account (+ confirm email)
' Use case: Register account (Authenticate account) · Actor: Guest
'
' Design patterns:
'   - Chain of responsibility: Express middleware (security headers → CORS → rateLimit) before the controller
'   - Decorator: action() wraps the controller with shared error handling (utils/action.ts)
'   - Unit of work: account + profile created in one transaction (db/transaction.ts withTransaction)
'   - Strategy + Factory + Dependency injection: «interface» Mailer (SmtpMailer / ConsoleMailer / MemoryMailer),
'     built by mailerFromConfig() and injected into the account security service (services/mail/mailer.ts)
'   - Repository: all SQL in repositories/*.repository.ts
' Lifelines use BCE stereotypes: «boundary» screens and outside services, «control» use-case logic (controllers,
' services, and the adapter interfaces in front of outside services), «entity» stored data (repository, stores);
' the database keeps its own symbol.
@startuml 01 Register account
title 1. Register account (+ confirm email)
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Guest
boundary "Web app" as Web
control "Middleware chain" as MW
control "Auth controller" as Ctrl
control "Auth service" as Svc
control "Account security\nservice" as Sec
control "«interface»\nMailer" as Mailer
entity "Repository" as Repo
database "Database" as DB
boundary "Email service" as Email

Guest -> Web : Fill in username, email, password
Web -> MW : POST /api/auth/register
note over MW : «Chain of responsibility»\nheaders → CORS → rateLimit\n(10 registrations an hour per network)
alt too many attempts
  MW --> Web : 429
end
MW -> Ctrl : register()
note over Ctrl : «Decorator» action():\nerrors → status + message
Ctrl -> Svc : register(input)
Svc -> Repo : registration open? find email / username
Repo -> DB : SELECT
alt email or username already used
  Svc --> Web : 400 "… already exists"
end
Svc -> Svc : hash password (bcrypt)
group «Unit of work» withTransaction()
  Svc -> Repo : create user + profile + gamification row
  Repo -> DB : INSERT …
end
Svc -> Sec : sendConfirmation(user)
Sec -> Repo : create link token (hash stored)
Repo -> DB : INSERT account_tokens
Sec -> Mailer : send(confirmation link)
note right of Mailer : «Strategy» chosen by\nmailerFromConfig():\nSMTP in production,\nconsole in development
Mailer -> Email : SMTP
Svc --> Ctrl : session token
Ctrl --> Web : 201 { token, user }
Web --> Guest : signed in → dashboard

== Later: the email link ==
Guest -> Web : open confirmation link
Web -> Ctrl : POST /api/auth/email/verify (token)
Ctrl -> Sec : verifyEmail(token)
Sec -> Repo : token valid, unused, newest? → mark used, address confirmed
Repo -> DB : UPDATE
Ctrl --> Web : confirmed
Web --> Guest : "Email confirmed"
@enduml
